    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d720">

                <pb facs="0935" n="925" xml:id="pg925"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.20 Missions/12–547: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-12-05T19:00:00-05:00">December 5, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1476. “From Sec State. Your reference in your 2327 Dec 3, 11 a.m. to
                    ‘experimental procedure, success at each, stage guiding future policy’ is not
                    understood and does not appear to be in consonance with second par of my 1436
                    Nov 28. Gen Barr’s status and responsibilities will be specifically defined and
                    delimited before his departure so that no misunderstanding should occur as to
                    character and extent of his activities. Needless to say I am glad that you are
                    not unhopeful that the Chinese leaders can make a revitalized effort. Biographic
                    sketch Gen Barr will be forwarded for transmission Gimo when action initiated
                    for his appointment.” [Marshall.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
